// SourceState WHETHER THE PROJECT'S SOURCE FOLDER IS STILL WHERE IT WAS — on a project made in a folder of
// your own (`createFlowProjectInOwnFolder`) or in a company folder
// (`createCompanyFlowProjectInFolder`), and absent on every other. A project in System → Flows is
// its folder, so it has no source to lose.
//
//   - `there` — a folder is at the source's place, and it holds a file.
//   - `empty` — a folder is at the source's place, and it holds no file: "A folder that still
//     exists and is empty is simply an empty project" (decision 0696).
//   - `gone` — no folder is at the source's place. The folder was moved, renamed or deleted in the
//     Storage app, and the project reads "Source is gone or empty".
//
// FLOWS KNOWS THE SOURCE BY ITS PLACE: the folders' names from the top of your own folders down,
// or from the top of the company's storage for a company project, compared as the Storage app
// compares a name. So a new folder made at the same place with the
// same name is the source again, and so is the old one brought back from Trash. It is read from
// the Storage app each time the project is answered; nothing in Flows remembers a move.
//
// `empty` IS NO FILE AT ALL, NOT NO FLOW. Which file is a flow is judged by reading it, and
// reading a file of your own waits on ONPLO-1497; until then a folder that holds only files Flows
// cannot read is `there`. A folder inside the source holds no file of it.
type SourceState string

