// ListDeployEnvironments The deploy environments
//
// WHERE A FLOW CAN BE PUT LIVE: every deploy environment somebody made. NONE IS READY-MADE
// (decision 0682), so the list starts empty; "Development" and "Production" are names the
// screen offers the first time a flow is put live, to take, change or skip. Not the account
// environment you switch between at the top of Onplo — a deploy environment is a place
// flows run, inside one of those.
//
// THIS PARAGRAPH SAID "Development and Production, which every account environment starts
// with" until 2026-10-05, a day after that decision; this file's own header already said
// none is.
//
// THIS IS WHERE THE ID A DEPLOY NAMES COMES FROM. `deployFlow`, `checkFlowDeploy` and the
// filters on `listDeployments` and `listRuns` each take a deploy environment by its id.
//
// AN ARCHIVED ONE IS STILL LISTED, and says so: it takes no new runs, the runs already going
// there finish, and a deploy into it is refused.
//
// THE PLACE A PERSONAL FLOW RUNS IS NEVER LISTED (decision 0870): "it is never shown or
// named". So in a personal account environment this list is empty, and a publish there names
// no deploy environment. THIS PARAGRAPH SAID "A PERSONAL ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT HAS THEM TOO"
// until 23 October 2026, when the spec lane handed over the ruling.
//
// Corresponds with GET /deploy-environments (the `ListDeployEnvironments` operationId).
func (c *Client) ListDeployEnvironments(ctx context.Context, params *ListDeployEnvironmentsParams, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*http.Response, error) {
	req, err := NewListDeployEnvironmentsRequest(c.Server, params)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	req = req.WithContext(ctx)
	if err := c.applyEditors(ctx, req, reqEditors); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return c.Client.Do(req)
}

// CreateDeployEnvironmentWithBody Add a deploy environment
//
// A NEW PLACE FLOWS CAN BE PUT LIVE, named when it is made. NONE IS READY-MADE (decision
// 0682): the first one somebody adds is the first there is, and it is ordinary like every
// later one.
//
// IT POINTS AT NO OBJECT, AND THAT IS A STATEMENT. A deploy environment sits in the account
// environment (decision 0761), so there is no container for "may I add one here" to be
// about, and the question is asked of the whole account environment.
//
// A NAME ANOTHER ONE CARRIES IS REFUSED with `name_taken`, and nothing is made. No two
// deploy environments of one account environment carry the same name, WHATEVER THE
// CAPITALS: "production" is refused where "Production" exists (decision 0759).
//
// EVERY PLAN INCLUDES TWO; MORE THAN TWO IS PREMIUM. A third one where the plan includes
// two is refused with `not_in_plan`, and nothing is made. The refusal says what is not
// included, in `not_included`: the feature "Additional environments", that Premium includes
// it, the two the plan allows and the two in use. It is never worded as a permission
// refusal, because no permission refused it (decision 0759).
//
// THE COMPANY'S SEAT LIFTS IT, whoever adds one. Deploy environments are a company's, so once
// one Flows Premium seat for company flows is held anywhere in the company, a third and
// every later one is made. Account is asked only when two are there already. Where Account
// cannot be asked who holds the seat, it is refused 503 with `account_unavailable`, and
// nothing is made: not known is not "not held".
//
// AN ARCHIVED ONE COUNTS as one of the two in use. It keeps its name and comes back with one
// click, and bringing it back asks nothing of the plan, so it still holds its place. Delete
// it to free the place.
//
// A PERSONAL ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT HAS NONE TO ADD. A published flow there runs in one place
// nobody names (decision 0870), so a request there is refused 409 with
// `deploy_environment_in_a_personal_environment`, and nothing is made. Where the
// authorization service did not say which kind of account environment the request is in,
// it is refused 503 with `authorization_unavailable`: ask again. Not known is not personal.
//
// THE PERMISSION IS ASKED FIRST. A caller who may not add a deploy environment is answered
// 403 and learns nothing about the plan.
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION. Adding one is not renaming, archiving or deleting one, and holding one
// of those is not holding this.
//
// NOT HERE: ITS COLOUR, for the reason a rename gives.
//
// AN ARCHIVED ONE'S NAME IS TAKEN: an archived one keeps its name.
//
// TOLD TO IDENTITY WHEN IT IS MADE, as the company's, in no container: what Keys reads when a
// key is attached to it (decision 0635).
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
// Corresponds with POST /deploy-environments (the `CreateDeployEnvironment` operationId).
func (c *Client) CreateDeployEnvironmentWithBody(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*http.Response, error) {
	req, err := NewCreateDeployEnvironmentRequestWithBody(c.Server, contentType, body)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	req = req.WithContext(ctx)
	if err := c.applyEditors(ctx, req, reqEditors); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return c.Client.Do(req)
}

