// CreateFlowProjectWithBody Make a flow project
//
// "+ New project": WHERE YOU BUILD, one per client, team or domain. Nothing is made for you,
// so a first flow needs one made first.
//
// IT IS NAMED WHEN IT IS MADE. The screen prefills a name on a person's first one; an API
// has no screen, so the request says the name.
//
// `owner_scope` SAYS WHOSE IT IS, AND IT NEVER CHANGES: `personal` is your own, in Personal
// flows; `company` is the company's, in Company flows.
//
// ITS FOLDER GOES TO SYSTEM → FLOWS, in the storage of whoever owns it — yours, or the
// company's. A project IS a folder in the storage tree, and the id answered here is that
// folder's id in the Storage app. Choosing a folder of your own for it is another operation,
// `createFlowProjectInOwnFolder`.
//
// IT POINTS AT NO OBJECT, AND THAT IS A STATEMENT. A project sits inside nothing, so there
// is no container for "may I make one here" to be about, and the question is asked of the
// whole account environment.
//
// A COMPANY PROJECT IS MADE ONLY WHERE THERE IS A COMPANY SIDE: a business account
// environment, or Onplo's own team (decision 0663). Asked for in a personal one, it is
// refused with a 422 whose error points at `/body/owner_scope` with the code
// `company_project_in_a_personal_environment`, and nothing is made. Where the authorization
// service did not say which kind of account environment the request is in, a company
// project is answered `authorization_unavailable` — ask again — and never that refusal: not
// known is not personal. A project of your own is made in any kind.
//
// NOTHING IS SHARED BY MAKING IT. A new project is private to you, or follows the company's
