// DeleteFlow Delete a flow
//
// THE FLOW GOES TO TRASH WITH ITS VERSIONS AND ITS RUN HISTORY: the account environment's
// one Trash, in the Storage app, where it waits for the keep-time. Nothing is erased by
// this call. From this call on it is answered as a flow that is not there, deleting it a
// second time is a 404, and its name is free in the project it left.
//
// A PART NOT BUILT, AND SO A 501: a delete asked by an agent or a machine. Trash names the
// person who deleted, and whom an agent works for is not known yet, so Storage sends nothing
// to Trash for one: this answers `not_implemented` and changes nothing (ONPLO-1209).
//
// A LIVE FLOW DOES NOT REFUSE IT. It stays live from the named version it was put live as,
// until it is taken off or replaced: Trash keeps that version meanwhile, whatever Trash's
// clock says (decision 0870). THIS REFUSED IT with `flow_is_live`, naming where, until
// 28 October 2026, when the Projects page ruled that it does not (ONPLO-3622).
//
// A LEGAL HOLD NEVER REFUSES IT (decision 0672).
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION. Deleting a flow and bringing one back are two acts, each a permission
// of its own.
//
// A RUN STILL GOING DOES NOT REFUSE IT. Taken out of every deploy environment, a flow with
// a run that has not ended is deleted, and the run finishes on the named version it runs
// on: Trash keeps that version until the run ends (ONPLO-3470). THIS SAID "NOT SAID YET"
// until 28 October 2026; the Projects page says it now (ONPLO-1567).
//
// BRINGING IT BACK IS `restoreFlow`.
//
// AN ARCHIVED FLOW CAN BE DELETED. Archiving sets a flow aside and deleting is the other
// half, on the same path as any other flow.
//
// Corresponds with DELETE /flows/{flow_id} (the `DeleteFlow` operationId).
func (c *Client) DeleteFlow(ctx context.Context, flowId FlowId, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*http.Response, error) {
	req, err := NewDeleteFlowRequest(c.Server, flowId)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	req = req.WithContext(ctx)
	if err := c.applyEditors(ctx, req, reqEditors); err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return c.Client.Do(req)
}

