// UnarchiveFlow Bring a flow back from the archive
//
// BACK IN THE FLOW LIST, exactly where it always was, and it can be saved, tested and put
// live again. Bringing it back puts nothing live: a flow was taken out of every deploy
// environment before it was archived, and it stays out until somebody puts it live.
//
// BRINGING BACK WHAT IS NOT ARCHIVED CHANGES NOTHING and answers the same.
//
// ONE FLOW INSIDE AN ARCHIVED PROJECT IS NOT BROUGHT BACK ALONE. The flow is archived because
// its project is, so saying it is back would be untrue: `409 flow_project_archived`, and
// nothing changes. `detail` names the project to bring back, which is the one the flow
// answers in `flow_project_id`. Answered since 2026-10-12: until then this case was a part
// not built and answered `not_implemented`.
//
// THE SAME PERMISSION AS ARCHIVING.
//
// AN AGENT OR A MACHINE BRINGS ONE BACK as a person does, as archiving says it. THIS
// ANSWERED 501 FOR ONE until 2026-10-15.
//
// Corresponds with DELETE /flows/{flow_id}/archive (the `UnarchiveFlow` operationId).
