// StartRunByHandWithBody Start a run of a live flow by hand
//
// "Run now": PICK WHERE IT RUNS, FILL IN THE START FORM, RUN. The run begins on the version
// live in that deploy environment and keeps it to the end, whatever is put live meanwhile.
//
// THE ANSWERS TO THE START FORM BECOME THE RUN'S TRIGGER DATA, each under its field's Key, "the
// variable name the answer becomes". The start form is the Manual trigger's, in the version
// live there. A flow whose trigger has no start form is sent no answers.
//
// ONE ANSWER PER FIELD THAT TAKES ONE, SAID WITH THE FIELD'S TYPE. A section heading and info
// text take none. An answer whose key the start form does not hold, whose type is not that
// field's, or a required field with no answer, is refused 422, each named by its pointer, and
// no run is made.
//
// A START FORM IS AS BIG AS ITS BUILDER MAKES IT (decision 0682). No number of answers and no
// length of text is ours: the one bound is what a single request may carry, and a body past it
// is refused 413.
//
// WHERE IT RUNS. The request names a deploy environment the flow is live in. No such deploy
// environment in this account environment is refused with `deploy_environment_not_found`, one
// the flow is not live in with `flow_not_live`, and an archived one, which takes no new runs,
// with `deploy_environment_archived`. In a personal account environment it is left out, as on
// `deployFlow` (decision 0870): the run goes where the flow is published. Left out anywhere
// else, it is refused with `deploy_environment_not_chosen`. Where identity did not say which
// kind of account environment this is, it is refused 503 with `authorization_unavailable`.
//
// A FLOW PAUSED THERE HOLDS THE RUN, AND DOES NOT REFUSE IT: "WHAT ARRIVES WHILE IT IS PAUSED IS
// HELD". The run is answered `queued`, waiting on `flow_paused`, and starts when the flow is
// resumed (ONPLO-2348).
//
// WHAT A RUN OF A FLOW WHOSE TRIGGER IS NOT MANUAL IS HANDED AS TRIGGER DATA is stated on no
// page, so nothing here promises it.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
//
