// ReplayRun Replay a failed run as a new run
//
// A REPLAY MAKES A NEW RUN CARRYING THE ORIGINAL TRIGGER DATA. The failed run stays as it
// is, and the new one says which run it replays (`replay_of_run_id`).
//
// CONNECTIONS ARE CALLED FOR REAL. Every step runs again from the trigger, including the
// ones that succeeded the first time — which is why the screen asks first, and why a replay
// is never automatic.
//
// ONLY A FAILED RUN IS REPLAYED (`run_not_failed`).
//
// THREE THINGS NO PAGE STATES, AND THIS CONTRACT'S OWN READING OF EACH (ONPLO-3784):
//   - IT RUNS ON THE FAILED RUN'S OWN NAMED VERSION, never the one live now: a replay re-runs
//     a past execution with its data, to debug it.
//   - IT RUNS IN THE FAILED RUN'S OWN DEPLOY ENVIRONMENT. One archived since takes no new
//     runs (`deploy_environment_archived`), and one deleted since is not there to run in
//     (`deploy_environment_not_found`).
//   - A FLOW PAUSED OR TAKEN OFF THERE DOES NOT STOP IT. Pausing a flow stops new triggers,
//     and a replay is a person's confirmed act, never a trigger.
//
