	// DeleteFlowProjectInOwnFolderWithResponse Delete a project made in a folder of your own, and keep the folder
	//
	// THE PROJECT LEAVES FLOWS AND ITS SOURCE FOLDER STAYS YOURS. Deleting a project whose source is
	// one of your own folders asks each time whether the folder stays or goes to Trash (decision
	// 0838). This is the first answer: the project is gone from Personal flows, and nothing in Storage
	// changes. The folder, and every file in it, stays where it is. From this call on the project is
	// not found, and deleting it a second time is a 404.
	//
	// NOTHING LIVE OR RUNNING REFUSES IT. What runs is a named version of the flow's file in the
	// Storage app's history, and the folder staying changes nothing for it (decision 0870).
	// Nor does `deleteFlowProject`, since 28 October 2026 (ONPLO-3622).
	//
	// THE SOURCE IS NOT ASKED ABOUT. A project whose source is there, empty or gone is deleted the same,
	// and Storage is asked nothing.
	//
	// ONLY A PROJECT MADE IN A FOLDER OF YOUR OWN IS DELETED HERE. A project in System → Flows is
	// deleted with `deleteFlowProject`, so its id is not found here, as no project of yours by that id
	// is found. A machine has no folders of its own, so no project of its is found either. An agent is
	// refused before that, with a 403: deleting a project is an act an agent asks a person to do
	// (decision 0794).
	//
	// ITS OWN PERMISSION, `flows:project.delete`, asked of the project, as on `deleteFlowProject`.
	//
	// SENDING THE FOLDER TO TRASH TOO, the other answer to the confirm, is
	// `deleteFlowProjectAndTrashItsFolder`, an operation of its own because it asks a second
	// permission, of the folder (decision 0831).
	//
	// NOT RULED, AND SO NOT HERE: bringing a deleted project of yours back. The folder is still yours,
	// and another project can take it as its source (`chooseFlowProjectSource`).
