	// CreateFlowWithBodyWithResponse Make a new flow
	//
	// "+ New flow", From scratch. The other two starting points on that dialog — With AI and
	// Templates — are not here yet.
	//
	// IT LANDS IN A PROJECT, ALWAYS, AND THE PROJECT IS NAMED. The project is what this
	// operation's permission is ABOUT: "may I make a flow here" is a question about the
	// container, so a role that lets you make flows in one project lets you make none in another.
	//
	// IT IS NAMED WHEN IT IS MADE. The screen prefills "New flow"; an API has no screen, so the
	// request says the name.
	//
	// A NEW FLOW ALREADY HOLDS A FILE. Every flow has exactly one trigger, and a new one starts
	// with a Manual trigger and nothing else. So a flow that was never saved still reopens, and
	// its first address reads a standard `.bpmn`.
	//
	// NOTHING RUNS. A flow runs only after it is deployed, and deploying is not here yet.
	//
	// A NAME ALREADY TAKEN IN THE PROJECT IS REFUSED with `name_taken`, and nothing is made. A
	// flow is a file in its project's folder, and two things in the same folder never carry the
	// same name. Two flows in two projects can share one. Capitals make no other name, and
	// neither does another spelling of an accented letter; a name is kept as you typed it
	// (ONPLO-1516). You give another.
	//
	// AN AGENT OR A MACHINE MAKES ONE as a person does. A new flow's file is saved under whose
	// rights the call ran: a person's own, a machine's own, and an agent's whoever it acts for,
	// a person or a team, never the agent itself. An agent the authorization service named
	// nobody for is answered `authorization_unavailable`, and nothing is made; ask again. THIS
	// ANSWERED 501 for an agent or a machine until 25 October 2026 (ONPLO-2100).
	//
	// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
