// CreateCompanyFlowProjectInFolderWithBodyWithResponse Make a company flow project in a company folder
//
// "+ New project" IN COMPANY FLOWS, WITH A FOLDER CHOSEN (decision 0869): the project's folder is
// made inside a folder of the company's, and that folder is the project's SOURCE, as a project in
// a folder of your own has one (decision 0696). Left empty in the dialog, the project goes where
// `createFlowProject` puts it: one that names no place is another operation (decision 0705, rule 6).
//
// `folder_id` IS WHERE THE PROJECT'S FOLDER GOES, never the project's folder itself: a new folder
// named `name` is made inside it. It is a folder of the company's, by its id in the Storage app.
// THE TOP OF THE COMPANY'S STORAGE IS NOT ONE: a folder there is asked who may open it, and making
// a project does not ask (Storage's `MakeFolderIn`). It is refused as a folder that is not there.
//
// THE SOURCE IS KNOWN BY ITS PLACE, as on a project of your own: the folders' names from the top
// of the company's storage down. The folder stays the company's in Storage, to move, rename or
// delete like any other, and Flows reads each time whether it is still there. STORAGE DOES NOT
// YET WARN before such a folder moves, nor offer to take the source along, as it does for a
// folder of your own (ONPLO-4578): until it does, a project whose folder was moved or renamed
// reads `gone`, and its source is chosen again.
//
// ITS ID IS THE PROJECT'S, NOT ITS FOLDER'S. The project outlives its folder, so its folder's id
// in Storage is not its id; it is answered as `source_folder_id`.
//
// IT IS THE COMPANY'S, and so it needs a company side (decision 0663): in a personal account
// environment it is refused with a 422 on `/body`, code `company_project_in_a_personal_environment`,
// and nothing is made. Where the authorization service did not say which kind of account
// environment the request is in, it is `authorization_unavailable` — ask again — and never that
// refusal: not known is not personal.
//
// AN AGENT OR A MACHINE MAKES ONE as a person does: the folder is the company's, not anybody's own.
//
// IT TAKES TWO PERMISSIONS, asked as one question (decision 0705): putting a folder in THAT
// folder, `storage:company-folder.create`, asked of `folder_id`; and making a project,
// `flows:project.create`, asked across the account environment, and satisfied only by a grant
// placed there. A refusal is one 403.
//
// A FOLDER THAT IS NOT THE COMPANY'S IS REFUSED with `folder_not_found`, and nothing is made. That
// covers no such folder, one in Trash, a file, the top of the company's storage, something on
// System Storage, and one in somebody's own folders, and the answer does not say which.
//
// A NAME ALREADY TAKEN IN THAT FOLDER IS REFUSED with `name_taken`, and nothing is made. Two
// things in the same folder never carry the same name; capitals make no other name, and neither
// does another spelling of an accented letter.
//
// A FOLDER TOO DEEP FOR A SOURCE IS REFUSED with `folder_too_deep`, as for a project of your own:
// a place names at most 64 folders, the new one last. The folder IS made and stays the company's,
// and no project is.
//
// NOTHING IS SHARED BY MAKING IT. Who sees it follows the company's roles, as for every company
// project; sharing the folder in Storage does not share the project (decision 0791).
//
// IT IS IN COMPANY FLOWS, `listFlowProjects` with `owner_scope=company`, for whoever may read it.
//
// ITS `source` IS `empty`: the folder was made in this call.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /company-flow-projects-in-folders (the `CreateCompanyFlowProjectInFolder` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) CreateCompanyFlowProjectInFolderWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*CreateCompanyFlowProjectInFolderResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.CreateCompanyFlowProjectInFolderWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseCreateCompanyFlowProjectInFolderResponse(rsp)
}

