// DeleteDeployEnvironmentWithResponse Delete a deploy environment
//
// THE DEPLOY ENVIRONMENT IS NO LONGER A PLACE A FLOW CAN BE PUT LIVE. From this call on it
// is answered as not there, and deleting it a second time is a 404.
//
// A DELETE IS FOR GOOD. A deploy environment is no file, so Trash never holds it, and nothing
// brings it back. Its name is free from this call on.
//
// AN ARCHIVED ONE IS DELETED AS IT IS: it need not be brought back first.
//
// REFUSED WHILE ANYTHING IS DEPLOYED THERE, AND THE REFUSAL SAYS HOW MANY. A flow live in it
// refuses the delete with `flow_is_live`, and `detail` says how many flows — "3 flows are
// live in Staging. Take each out first." Take each out with `undeployFlow`.
//
// REFUSED WHILE A RUN THERE IS STILL GOING, AND THE REFUSAL SAYS HOW MANY: `run_is_going`. A
// run is still going while it is queued, running or paused. Live is answered before running.
// THIS SAID "THE RULE A FLOW PROJECT'S DELETE HAS" until 28 October 2026, when a project's
// delete stopped refusing a run (ONPLO-3622). This one stands on the configuration guide's own
// sentence, "Delete is also blocked while any run here is still going".
//
// ITS FINISHED RUNS STAY IN THE RUN HISTORY, and each still reads the name it ran in: a
// `Run`'s `deploy_environment_name`. Its `deploy_environment_id` then names nothing that is
// listed.
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION, as renaming and archiving are.
//
// NOT HERE: WHAT WAS ATTACHED TO IT. A key, a secret or a variable's value given to a deploy
// environment is a Keys entry in the vault. What becomes of each when the deploy environment
// goes is the vault's to say. Which connection an alias uses there is Flows' own
// (`bindDeployEnvironmentConnection`, ONPLO-3655). THIS PARAGRAPH SAID THE
// BINDING WAS INTEGRATIONS' until 31 October 2026; the spec lane ruled it Flows' on
// 28 October 2026.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with DELETE /deploy-environments/{deploy_environment_id} (the `DeleteDeployEnvironment` operationId).
