// CreateFlowProjectInOwnFolderWithBodyWithResponse Make a flow project in a folder of your own
//
// "+ New project" IN PERSONAL FLOWS, WITH A FOLDER CHOSEN: the project's folder is made
// inside one of your own folders, and that folder is the project's SOURCE (decision 0696).
// Left empty in the dialog, the project goes to System → Flows, and that is
// `createFlowProject`: one that names no place is another operation (decision 0705, rule 6).
//
// `folder_id` IS WHERE THE PROJECT'S FOLDER GOES, never the project's folder itself: a new
// folder named `name` is made inside it. It is one of your own folders, or the tree's id for
// the top of your own folders, as in the Storage app's "Create a folder".
//
// THE SOURCE IS KNOWN BY ITS PLACE, AND STAYS YOURS. The new folder is an ordinary folder of
// yours: in Storage you may move, rename or delete it, and move a single flow out of it.
// Flows remembers WHERE it is, by the folders' names. Storage warns you first, and on a move or
// a rename asks whether the project should follow. A folder made later at the same place with
// the same name is the source again, and so is the old one brought back from Trash.
//
// ITS ID IS THE PROJECT'S, NOT ITS FOLDER'S. A project in System → Flows IS its folder and shares
// its id. This one outlives its folder, so it has an id of its own, and its folder's id in
// Storage is not answered.
//
// IT IS ALWAYS YOUR OWN. A company project goes to System → Flows of the company's storage; whether
// one may go to a chosen company folder is not decided. So the request carries no
// `owner_scope`, and an agent or a machine is refused with a 422 on `/body/folder_id`, code
// `personal_project_without_a_person`: there is no person whose folders it would go in.
//
// IT TAKES TWO PERMISSIONS, asked as one question (decision 0705): putting a folder in THAT
// folder, `storage:own-folder.create`, asked of `folder_id`; and making a project,
// `flows:project.create`, asked across the account environment, and satisfied only by a
// grant placed there. A refusal is one 403.
//
// A FOLDER THAT IS NOT ONE OF YOURS IS REFUSED with `folder_not_found`, and nothing is made.
// That covers no such folder, one in Trash, a file, something on System Storage, and one in a
// colleague's tree, and the answer does not say which.
//
// A NAME ALREADY TAKEN IN THAT FOLDER IS REFUSED with `name_taken`, and nothing is made. Two
// things in the same folder never carry the same name; capitals make no other name, and neither
// does another spelling of an accented letter. Two projects of yours in two different folders
// may share a name.
//
// A FOLDER TOO DEEP FOR A SOURCE IS REFUSED with `folder_too_deep`. A place names at most 64
// folders, the new one last, so a project's folder made inside a folder 64 folders down from
// the top of yours has no place Flows can remember. Storage does not know the depth before it makes the folder, so
// the folder IS made and stays yours in Storage, and no project is. Choose a folder higher
// up; asked again in the same folder, the name is taken by the folder that was made.
//
// NOTHING IS SHARED BY MAKING IT. Sharing the folder does not share the project either: a
// project is shared only from Flows (decision 0791).
//
// IT IS IN YOUR PERSONAL FLOWS, `listFlowProjects`, as it was answered here.
//
// ITS `source` IS `empty`: the folder was made in this call. The list says it again each time it
// is read, because you may move, rename or delete the folder in the Storage app.
//
// ANOTHER FOLDER OF YOURS MAY BE ITS SOURCE LATER: `chooseFlowProjectSource`. IT COULD NOT BE
// POINTED AT ANOTHER FOLDER until 17 October 2026. IT DID NOT SAY
// WHETHER ITS SOURCE WAS THERE, EMPTY OR GONE until that day. IT WAS IN NO LIST until the
// same day. THIS ANSWERED
// `501 not_implemented` until 17 October 2026, while the shipped server neither made the folder
// (ONPLO-2601) nor handed Flows' door the call that makes it.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /flow-projects-in-own-folders (the `CreateFlowProjectInOwnFolder` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) CreateFlowProjectInOwnFolderWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*CreateFlowProjectInOwnFolderResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.CreateFlowProjectInOwnFolderWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseCreateFlowProjectInOwnFolderResponse(rsp)
}

