// DeleteFlowProjectAndTrashItsFolderWithBodyWithResponse Delete a project made in a folder of your own, and send the folder to Trash
//
// THE PROJECT LEAVES FLOWS AND ITS SOURCE FOLDER GOES TO TRASH. Deleting a project whose source is
// one of your own folders asks each time whether the folder stays or goes to Trash (decision
// 0838). This is the second answer. The folder and everything in it go to the Storage app's one
// Trash, exactly as your own delete of it there would, and wait out the keep-time. The first
// answer, keeping the folder, is `deleteFlowProjectInOwnFolder`.
//
// YOU NAME THE FOLDER YOU SAW. `folder_id` is the project's `source_folder_id` as the list or the
// project answered it. A folder that is no longer what is at the project's source, because it
// was moved or renamed in the Storage app since, is refused with `folder_is_not_the_source`.
// Nothing changes, and the confirm is asked again. A source that is gone has no folder to send:
// delete the project with `deleteFlowProjectInOwnFolder`.
//
// THE FOLDER FIRST, THEN THE PROJECT. When the Storage app refuses the folder, the project stays
// too. A file in the folder that an app is using refuses the whole delete with `in_use`, whose
// `detail` names the file by its id, as the Storage app's own delete does. When the folder is in
// Trash and the project could not be removed, asking again answers `folder_is_not_the_source`, and
// `deleteFlowProjectInOwnFolder` finishes it.
