// one is kept in Trash until its flow is stopped or replaced, so the flow keeps running (decision
// 0870).
//
// TWO PERMISSIONS, EACH ASKED OF ITS OWN OBJECT (decision 0838). Deleting the project,
// `flows:project.delete`, is asked of the project. Deleting the folder, `storage:own-folder.delete`,
// is asked of the folder you name. A refusal of the first is one 403. A folder you may not delete
// answers as one that is not yours: `folder_not_found`, and nothing changes.
//
// ONLY A PROJECT MADE IN A FOLDER OF YOUR OWN IS DELETED HERE, as on `deleteFlowProjectInOwnFolder`.
// A project in System → Flows, a machine's and an id no project of yours has are not found. An agent
// is refused before that, with a 403: deleting a project is an act an agent asks a person to do
// (decision 0794).
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
