// ListFlowsInOwnFolderWithResponse The flows in a project made in a folder of your own
//
// WHAT THE PROJECT'S FLOWS TAB SHOWS, FOR A PROJECT WHOSE SOURCE IS ONE OF YOUR OWN FOLDERS. Its
// flows are the files in that folder (decision 0696), however they got there: made here with
// `createFlowInOwnFolder`, uploaded or moved in through the Storage app. A project in System →
// Flows lists its flows with `listFlows`.
//
// READ FROM THE FOLDER EACH TIME. The list is what is in the folder now, a page at a time, in
// the Storage app's order. A file moved out of the folder in the Storage app is no flow of the
// project from then on, and one moved in is.
//
// THE FILES DIRECTLY IN THE FOLDER, never what sits in a folder inside it, and only the files
// Flows can read: a file whose bytes are XML, as the Storage app judged them at its last save.
// The kind is read from the bytes, never the name, so a flow named with no `.bpmn` ending is
// listed. A note, an image or a file made empty in the Storage app stays in the folder and is
// not listed. A page may come back shorter than `limit`, and `next_cursor` still continues it.
//
// A SOURCE THAT IS GONE LISTS NOTHING: an empty page. The project says its source is `gone`, and
// another folder can be chosen (`chooseFlowProjectSource`).
//
// NO FLOW HERE IS ARCHIVED. A file in a folder of yours is not archived in Flows, so every flow
// answers `archived` false, and the list takes no `include_archived`.
//
// ONE PERMISSION, `flows:flow.read`, ASKED OF THE PROJECT, as `listFlows` asks it. The files are
// yours, in a folder of yours, so no row is asked anything more: what is only yours is seen
// without a permission (decision 0811, rule 4).
//
// ONLY A PROJECT MADE IN A FOLDER OF YOUR OWN IS LISTED HERE. A project in System → Flows, a
// colleague's and an id no project of yours has are not found, and so is every project asked by an
// agent or a machine: neither has folders of its own.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with GET /flow-projects-in-own-folders/{flow_project_id}/flows (the `ListFlowsInOwnFolder` operationId).
