// ChooseFlowProjectSourceWithResponse Choose another folder of your own as a project's source
//
// "SOURCE IS GONE OR EMPTY" — PICK ANOTHER FOLDER, under the project's Source files in Personal flows
// (decision 0696). A project made in a folder of your own knows its source by its PLACE. After the
// folder is moved, renamed or deleted in Storage, you choose another existing folder of yours,
// and the project's source is that folder from now on. This is one operation, and it is the only
// way the source changes by your own choice. A move made in Storage changes it only when you
// say there that the project should follow.
//
// NOTHING IS MADE, MOVED OR COPIED. The folder stays where it is, with what is in it. A file Flows
// can read in it is a flow of the project, however it got there. The old place is forgotten, and a
// folder made later at that place is no source of this project.
//
// THE PROJECT KEEPS EVERYTHING ELSE: its id, its name, and that it is yours. Its name is its own and
// does not become the folder's.
//
// TWO PERMISSIONS, EACH ASKED OF ITS OWN OBJECT (decision 0705, rule 7). Changing the project,
// `flows:project.change`, is asked of the project. Putting things in the chosen folder,
// `storage:own-folder.change`, is asked of the folder: once it is the source, Flows saves flows
// into it. A refusal is one 403.
//
// ONLY A PROJECT MADE IN A FOLDER OF YOUR OWN HAS A SOURCE TO CHOOSE. A project in System → Flows
// is managed only in Flows and has no source folder, so its id is not found here, as no project of
// yours by that id is found.
//
// A FOLDER THAT IS NOT ONE OF YOURS IS REFUSED with `folder_not_found`, and nothing changes. That
// covers no such folder, one in Trash, a file, the top of your own folders, a folder in the System
// zone, one in a colleague's tree, and one deeper than a place names (64 folders). The answer does
// not say which.
//
// THE FOLDER IT ALREADY HAS IS ITS OWN: choosing it again changes nothing and refuses nothing.
//
// A MACHINE IS REFUSED with a 422 on `/body/folder_id`, code `personal_project_without_a_person`,
// as on `createFlowProjectInOwnFolder`: there is no person whose folders it would be in. An agent is
// refused before that, with a 403: changing a project is an act an agent asks a person to do
// (decision 0794).
//
// THE ANSWER SAYS THE SOURCE AS THE LIST DOES: `there` or `empty`, read from what Storage says is
// at the new place. A folder moved away in the moment between the two is `gone`.
//
// Takes a body of the `application/json` content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PUT /flow-projects-in-own-folders/{flow_project_id}/source (the `ChooseFlowProjectSource` operationId).
