// DeleteFlowProjectWithResponse Delete a flow project
//
// THE PROJECT'S FOLDER AND EVERYTHING IN IT GO TO TRASH, where they wait for the keep-time
// like any deleted folder. Nothing is erased by this call. The account environment has one
// Trash, in the Storage app, and a project comes back from it whole or not at all. From this
// call on the project and every flow of it are answered as not there, and deleting it a
// second time is a 404.
//
// NOTHING LIVE OR RUNNING REFUSES IT. "A live flow or a running run refuses neither choice,
// because what runs is the named version it was put live as, and Trash keeps that version
// until the flow is stopped or replaced" (the Projects page, decision 0870). A live flow runs
// on from the version its deployment holds, and a run still going finishes from the version
// it holds itself (ONPLO-3470). THIS REFUSED BOTH, with `flow_is_live` and `run_is_going`,
// until 28 October 2026 (ONPLO-3622).
//
// A LEGAL HOLD NEVER REFUSES IT (decision 0672). THIS SAID THE STORAGE PAGE STILL LISTED A
// HOLD AMONG WHAT BLOCKS until 2026-10-11; the page says "A legal hold never blocks it" now.
//
// A PART NOT BUILT, AND SO A 501: a delete asked by an agent or a machine. Trash names the
// person who deleted, and whom an agent works for is not known yet, so Storage sends nothing
// to Trash for one: this answers `not_implemented` and changes nothing (ONPLO-1209).
//
// THE KEEP-TIME IS THE ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT'S OWN, set once in Storage for everything in
// Trash. Nothing here sets it or answers it.
//
// ITS OWN PERMISSION, as making and renaming are (decision 0651).
//
// NOT HERE: BRINGING A DELETED PROJECT BACK. It is restored from Storage's Trash. The
// restore the catalogue gives Flows is of a deleted FLOW.
//
// NOT HERE: A PROJECT PLACED IN A FOLDER OF YOUR OWN. That one is deleted with
// `deleteFlowProjectInOwnFolder` or `deleteFlowProjectAndTrashItsFolder`, where nothing live
// refuses it either (decision 0870).
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with DELETE /flow-projects/{flow_project_id} (the `DeleteFlowProject` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) DeleteFlowProjectWithResponse(ctx context.Context, flowProjectId FlowProjectId, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*DeleteFlowProjectResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.DeleteFlowProject(ctx, flowProjectId, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseDeleteFlowProjectResponse(rsp)
}

// RenameFlowProjectWithBodyWithResponse Rename a flow project
//
// RENAMING A PROJECT RENAMES ITS FOLDER IN STORAGE. They are one thing — the project IS
// that folder — so there is one name, and this is where it is changed.
//
// A RENAME CHANGES NOTHING ELSE. The project keeps its id, whose it is, and every flow
