// CreateFlowWithBodyWithResponse Make a new flow
//
// "+ New flow", From scratch. The other two starting points on that dialog — With AI and
// Templates — are not here yet.
//
// IT LANDS IN A PROJECT, ALWAYS, AND THE PROJECT IS NAMED. The project is what this
// operation's permission is ABOUT: "may I make a flow here" is a question about the
// container, so a role that lets you make flows in one project lets you make none in another.
//
// IT IS NAMED WHEN IT IS MADE. The screen prefills "New flow"; an API has no screen, so the
// request says the name.
//
// A NEW FLOW ALREADY HOLDS A FILE. Every flow has exactly one trigger, and a new one starts
// with a Manual trigger and nothing else. So a flow that was never saved still reopens, and
// its first address reads a standard `.bpmn`.
