// flow is a file in its project's folder, and two things in the same folder never carry the
// same name. Two flows in two projects can share one. Capitals make no other name, and
// neither does another spelling of an accented letter; a name is kept as you typed it
// (ONPLO-1516). You give another.
//
// AN AGENT OR A MACHINE MAKES ONE as a person does. A new flow's file is saved under whose
// rights the call ran: a person's own, a machine's own, and an agent's whoever it acts for,
// a person or a team, never the agent itself. An agent the authorization service named
// nobody for is answered `authorization_unavailable`, and nothing is made; ask again. THIS
// ANSWERED 501 for an agent or a machine until 25 October 2026 (ONPLO-2100).
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
