// ShareFlowProjectWithBodyWithResponse Share a flow project
//
// SHARING IS CONTAINER-FIRST: "a shared project brings its flows, forms, decisions, tables and
// their running instances with it". The share is placed on the project, and the role reaches
// everything inside it; a grant placed on one of them "can only add to that, never take away".
//
// ONE OF FOUR ROLES — Viewer, Commenter, Editor, Manager — each the register's
// `flows.role.<this word>`. WHAT EACH ROLE LETS ITS HOLDER DO IS NOT ON A PAGE YET: the
// register says "no Flows page maps a role onto View, Design, Create, Deploy and Run". A share
// can be placed before that day, and it reaches only what its role then holds.
//
// WITH A MEMBER OR A TEAM OF THIS ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT. Nobody by that id here, or no such team,
// is refused (409 `recipient_not_found`). SHARING WITH AN EXTERNAL GUEST IS NOT HERE YET. The
// page names guests, and a share outside the account environment asks Account's permission as
// well (decision 0658), so `recipient.kind` has no word for an outside person until that half
// is declared — one more word then, and no new shape.
//
// A BUSINESS ACCOUNT ENVIRONMENT ONLY, as the catalogue gives the act. A personal one has no
// member but its own person, so from there every share would be with an outside person, and
// it waits with that half. A project of your own in a business account environment is shared
// as a company one is.
//
// SHARING AGAIN CHANGES THE SHARE THAT IS THERE. A holder has one grant per object (decision
// 0650), so a person or a team shared with again takes the new role and the new end and keeps
// the id. `created` says which it was and the status is `200` either way: a retry after a
// timeout reads `false` and the same share, never a second one.
//
// `access_until` IS THE MOMENT THIS SHARE ENDS, and the time zone it was chosen in (decision
// 0650). Left out, the share has no end. A moment that has already passed is refused (422
// naming `access_until`, `access_until_passed`).
//
// KEEP THE SHARE'S ID: it is what changes or ends this share later. The list of what you
// shared, Shared with others, is not declared here.
//
// NOBODY IS TOLD BY THIS CALL. Flows' Notification preferences page lists no event for a
// project shared with you, so there is nothing to post under.
//
// WHO MAY SHARE IT: whoever holds `flows:project.share` on the project.
//
// NEVER AN AI AGENT'S TO DO, and never a raw key's: a share is a grant of access (403
// `ring_requires_person`).
//
// THE IDENTITY SERVICE KEEPS THE GRANT, AND WRITES IT ITSELF. When it cannot be reached, 503
// `identity_unavailable`: whether the share landed is not known, so send the same request
// again. It is the same act, and answers the share that is there.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /flow-projects/{flow_project_id}/grants (the `ShareFlowProject` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) ShareFlowProjectWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, flowProjectId FlowProjectId, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*ShareFlowProjectResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.ShareFlowProjectWithBody(ctx, flowProjectId, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseShareFlowProjectResponse(rsp)
}

