// DeleteFlowInOwnFolderWithResponse Delete a flow in a folder of your own
//
// "DELETE FLOW: THE FILE GOES TO STORAGE'S TRASH." A flow of a project made in a folder of your own
// is an ordinary file in that folder (decision 0696), so deleting it is the Storage app's own delete
// of the file: it waits in the account environment's one Trash for the keep-time, and comes back
// from there or through `restoreFlowInOwnFolder`. Nothing is erased by this call. A flow in System
// → Flows is deleted with `deleteFlow`.
//
// THE FILE IS YOURS, SO ITS PERMISSION IS THE FILE'S. A flow in a folder of yours answers to the
// folder's permissions and never to a project's (decision 0696): this asks `storage:own-file.delete`
// of the file, as deleting it in the Storage app asks. No project is named, and none is asked: a
// file moved to another folder of yours is deleted the same.
//
// FROM THIS CALL ON IT IS NOT THERE. It leaves the project's flows, and opening, saving or deleting
// it again answers `flow_not_found`. Its name is free in the folder it left.
//
// A FILE AN APP IS USING IS REFUSED WITH `in_use`, whose `detail` names the file by its id, as the
// Storage app's own delete refuses it. Nothing goes to Trash. A flow in System → Flows is not
// refused for being live (`deleteFlow`); a file of yours is held by the Storage app's rule, because
// this is that app's delete. No flow in a folder can be put live yet (ONPLO-4577), so no flow of
// Flows' meets it today.
//
// NO FILE OF YOURS BY THAT ID IS ONE ANSWER, `flow_not_found`: a folder, a file already in Trash, a
// colleague's file, one on System Storage, and an id nobody minted.
//
// A PART NOT BUILT, AND SO A 501: a delete asked by an agent or a machine. Trash names the person
// who deleted, and whom an agent works for is not known yet, so the Storage app sends nothing of a
// person's own to Trash for one: this answers `not_implemented` and changes nothing (ONPLO-1209).
//
// ONE CHANGE IS RECORDED, naming the flow, about you, once the Storage app has sent it.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with DELETE /flows-in-own-folders/{flow_id} (the `DeleteFlowInOwnFolder` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) DeleteFlowInOwnFolderWithResponse(ctx context.Context, flowId FlowId, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*DeleteFlowInOwnFolderResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.DeleteFlowInOwnFolder(ctx, flowId, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseDeleteFlowInOwnFolderResponse(rsp)
}

