// PauseDeploymentWithResponse Pause a live flow
//
// PAUSE: THE FLOW STOPS ACCEPTING NEW TRIGGERS THERE WHILE RUNS ALREADY GOING FINISH — the
// maintenance case and the 2am case. It stays live: the same version is still the one there.
//
// WHAT ARRIVES WHILE IT IS PAUSED IS HELD, NOT REFUSED. A trigger that comes in is accepted
// and waits as a queued run that says why (`queued_because: flow_paused`), and starts when
// the flow is resumed.
//
// RUNS ALREADY GOING ARE NOT TOUCHED. Read them with `listRuns`; pausing or stopping one is
// its own act on the run.
//
