//
// ITS PERMISSION IS ABOUT THE FLOW WHERE IT IS LIVE — a deployment — and not about the flow
// itself. It named `flows:flow.suspend` until the catalogue gave pausing a live flow a row
// of its own, so that suspending a FLOW can mean archiving it.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with PUT /flows/{flow_id}/deployments/{deploy_environment_id}/pause (the `PauseDeployment` operationId).
