// RestoreFlowVersionWithResponse Restore an earlier version of a flow
//
// AN EARLIER VERSION COMES BACK AS THE NEWEST SAVE: "an earlier version comes back from
// History & restore as the newest save". The named version itself stays as it was, and so
// does every run and deployment that uses it.
//
// NOTHING IS PUT LIVE. The restored save is the flow as it is edited; putting it live is
// `deployFlow`, which names a version of its own.
//
// A VERSION OF ANOTHER FILE, OR NONE, answers as one that does not exist.
//
// THE VERSION THAT IS ALREADY THE NEWEST SAVE changes nothing, and the flow is answered as it is.
//
// AN ARCHIVED FLOW IS READ, NOTHING ELSE (decision 0700): it is brought back before a version is
// restored into it (`flow_archived`).
//
